408	  <h2 class="h">The headline</h2>
409	  <div class="callout">
410	    <span class="callout-label">Every dollar figure is suspect</span>
411	    <p><code>PricingTable::rate_for</code> matches model names by exact string equality. No adapter normalizes a raw provider string (<code>claude-opus-4-20250514</code>, <code>gemini-2.0-flash-001</code>) to the short seeded key (<code>claude-opus</code>, <code>gemini-2.0-flash</code>) before calling it. Every one of those misses falls through the "unrecognized model" guard and gets billed at Claude 3.5 Sonnet's rate — silently, with no warning or log line.</p>
412	    <p>This was verified by direct execution, not inference: <code>rate_for("claude-3-5-haiku-20241022", ...)</code>, <code>rate_for("claude-opus-4-20250514", ...)</code>, <code>rate_for("gpt-4o-2024-08-06", ...)</code>, and <code>rate_for("gemini-2.0-flash-001", ...)</code> all return Sonnet's <code>$3.00 / $3.75 / $0.30 / $15.00</code> per-M rates. Claude 3.5 Sonnet is the only model priced correctly today, and only by coincidence — it's the fallback target.</p>
413	  </div>
414	  <p>A second, independent bug compounds it: any Codex session that reports a <code>service_tier</code> (the fixture itself carries one) prices the <em>entire session at $0.00</em>, because the pricing table has no tiered rows and the tier filter simply finds nothing to match.</p>
