437	    <div class="f-body"><p><code>PricingTable::seed()</code> pushes every row with <code>tier: None</code>. When a Codex payload sets <code>tier: Some("Standard")</code>, the tier-equality filter matches zero rows for all four rate kinds, and <code>unwrap_or(0.0)</code> silently returns $0.00. The shipped Codex test fixture carries <code>service_tier: "Standard"</code> — a real session, priced at zero, and the test never asserts the cost.</p>
438	    <details class="f-more"><summary>Fix</summary><div class="f-more-body">
439	      <p>Fall back to the <code>tier: None</code> row when no tiered row matches, and consider making <code>rate_for</code> return <code>Option&lt;f64&gt;</code> so an unpriceable combination is visible to the caller instead of collapsing to zero.</p>
