458	    <div class="f-title">A structural type gap, not a local bug — two accumulators built on a state the system never reaches</div>
459	    <div class="f-body"><p><code>CanonicalTurn</code> can hold both <code>tool_calls</code> and <code>tool_results</code>, but no adapter ever populates both on the same turn — a call and its result always land on separate turns. Two accumulators correlate the two <em>within one turn</em> and therefore always produce a constant: <code>TrajectoryDagAccumulator</code>'s <code>had_error</code> is <code>false</code> for every node in every real session, and <code>PrLinkAccumulator</code>'s <code>linked_via_vcs_tool</code> is always <code>0</code>. A test at <code>test_accumulators.rs:1447</code> asserts the always-false behavior as if it were intended.</p>
460	    <details class="f-more"><summary>Why this is architectural, not a patch</summary><div class="f-more-body">
461	      <p>Patching these two call sites individually won't stop the next accumulator from making the same reasonable-looking assumption against the same type. The fix belongs at the <code>CanonicalTranscript</code> model level — a cross-turn <code>call_id</code> correlation pass, run once by an adapter or a shared post-processing step, not re-derived per accumulator.</p>
462	    </div></details>
