The gate `if in_tok > 0 || out_tok > 0` never inspects `c_write`/`c_read`. A usage object reporting ONLY cache activity (e.g. `input_tokens: 0, output_tokens: 0, cache_read_input_tokens: 5000` -- a genuine pure cache-hit turn) fails the gate entirely, so the real 5000-token cache read is silently never recorded anywhere -- `turn_usage` stays `None`, and none of the four running totals are incremented, undercounting `cache_hit_ratio` and `total_cost_usd`.

## The fix

Read the CURRENT exact code first (line numbers may have shifted from other fixes this session). Widen the gate to include the cache fields: `if in_tok > 0 || out_tok > 0 || c_write > 0 || c_read > 0`.

