## The bug

`crates/lumen-analysis/src/accumulators/context_growth.rs`: `ContextGrowthAccumulator.previous_prompt_tokens` is a plain `u64` (line 18), defaulting to 0 via `#[derive(Default)]`. The growth-detection guard (line 36):
```rust
if prompt > self.previous_prompt_tokens && self.previous_prompt_tokens > 0 {
```
uses `self.previous_prompt_tokens > 0` to mean "we've seen a real previous turn" -- but this conflates the type's default-zero (genuinely "no previous turn yet") with a REAL previous turn whose prompt_tokens happened to be exactly 0 (a legitimate reading, not absence of data). Concretely: a three-turn sequence with real `prompt_tokens()` values `[500, 0, 5000]` -- after turn 2 (prompt=0), `previous_prompt_tokens` becomes `0`. On turn 3 (prompt=5000), the guard `5000 > 0 && 0 > 0` evaluates the second clause as FALSE, so the real 4500-token-equivalent jump from turn 2 to turn 3 is silently never recorded in `total_growth`/`max_jump_tokens`, even though it's a genuine, large jump. Note the file ALREADY has the correct pattern one field over -- `initial_prompt_tokens: Option<u64>` (line 17) correctly uses `None`/`is_none()` to distinguish "unset" from "real zero" (lines 32-34) -- `previous_prompt_tokens` just never got the same treatment.

