Change `previous_prompt_tokens: u64` to `previous_prompt_tokens: Option<u64>` (mirroring `initial_prompt_tokens`'s existing correct pattern in the same struct). Update `update()`'s growth-detection logic:
```rust
if let Some(prev) = self.previous_prompt_tokens {
    if prompt > prev {
        let jump = prompt - prev;
        self.total_growth += jump;
        self.max_jump_tokens = self.max_jump_tokens.max(jump);
    }
}
self.previous_prompt_tokens = Some(prompt);
```
(replacing the old combined `if prompt > self.previous_prompt_tokens && self.previous_prompt_tokens > 0 { ... } ... self.previous_prompt_tokens = prompt;` block). This correctly means: on the very first usage-bearing turn, there's no previous value (`None`), so no growth is computed (correct, matches existing first-turn behavior) -- but from the SECOND turn onward, `previous_prompt_tokens` is always `Some(actual_value)`, even if that actual value happens to be 0, so a real zero-to-nonzero jump is no longer silently skipped.

