Workspace: /Users/gabe/Projects/lumen. Baseline: 27 fixes landed (cb29996..1ec1008), `cargo test --workspace` green (161 tests), `just ci` passes end-to-end.

## The finding

`AnalyticsEngine::process_transcript` (crates/lumen-analysis/src/engine.rs, lines 98-153) runs all 19 accumulators over every turn. For each subagent transcript, it recursively calls `AnalyticsEngine::new().process_transcript(subagent)` -- computing the FULL 19-accumulator report -- but then only keeps `sub_report.attribution` (line 126: `by_subagent.insert(key, sub_report.attribution);`), discarding circuit_breaker/api_health/autonomy/stats/trajectory_dag/etc. entirely. This is real, avoidable computational waste: 18 of 19 accumulators run to completion for every subagent purely to be thrown away.

## The fix

Extract a lightweight helper that runs ONLY `AttributionAccumulator` (the sole accumulator whose subagent output survives), and use it in the subagent loop instead of the full recursive `process_transcript` call:

```rust
/// Runs only the attribution accumulator over a transcript's turns. `process_transcript`'s
/// `by_subagent` map only ever keeps a subagent's `.attribution` field (see below), so running
/// the other 18 accumulators to completion for every subagent, only to discard their output,
/// was pure waste -- this is the minimal equivalent computation.
fn attribution_only(transcript: &CanonicalTranscript) -> AttributionMetrics {
    let mut attribution = AttributionAccumulator::default();
    for turn in &transcript.turns {
        attribution.update(turn);
    }
    attribution.finalize()
}
```

Then change the subagent loop (lines 121-127) from:
```rust
let mut by_subagent = BTreeMap::new();
for subagent in &transcript.subagents {
    let sub_report = AnalyticsEngine::new().process_transcript(subagent);
    let key = subagent.subagent_role.clone().unwrap_or_else(|| CompactString::from(subagent.session_id.as_str()));
    by_subagent.insert(key, sub_report.attribution);
}
```
to:
```rust
let mut by_subagent = BTreeMap::new();
for subagent in &transcript.subagents {
    let key = subagent.subagent_role.clone().unwrap_or_else(|| CompactString::from(subagent.session_id.as_str()));
    by_subagent.insert(key, Self::attribution_only(subagent));
}
```

This is behaviorally IDENTICAL for `by_subagent`'s contents (both old and new code only ever populate it with `AttributionMetrics` computed purely from `AttributionAccumulator::update`/`finalize` over the subagent's own turns -- the full recursive call's other 18 accumulator outputs and its own `by_subagent`/nested-subagent handling were already discarded one level up, so removing them changes nothing observable) -- it's a pure computation-reduction, not a behavior change. Read the CURRENT exact code in crates/lumen-analysis/src/engine.rs first to confirm line numbers/structure and `AttributionAccumulator`'s exact import path/type before editing.

